{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793739160,"nonce":"w5YsFr5kNALRwCPo+GR+yjd3V9w=","title":"Tiered interpreter waits for static-loop optimization before its first call","message":"Parent: e8fe1d316aba9fd0ba51fcbcb04b6296e23703113d633f46ef41f045c4eff5f4\n\nA lazy user function classified by hot_static_loop is queued at module load and its interpreter tick waits for optimized native code on the first invocation. This bypasses the existing lowered-HIR interpreter path, which requires release insertion but not the full optimizer. On the prior method_call NUC trace, the main-thread wait was about 11.33 ms.\n\nRemove the eager static-hot compile request and first-entry wait. Interpret lowered HIR, retain correctness-required releases, then use observed invocation/backedge heat to request native compilation and OSR. Preserve native library snapshot loading and the shared optimized body for subsequent native tiers. Validate interpreter entry, active-frame transfer, Lua behavior, the complete pinned TypeScript corpus, and frozen-binary NUC wall/kernel comparisons.","files":null}]}